title: "fix(txpool): handle AlreadyImported race in fork-aware submit_and_watch"

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    Fixes a race condition in the fork-aware transaction pool where
    `submit_and_watch` can spuriously return `AlreadyImported` (RPC error 1013)
    even though only a single submission was made. This happens when a concurrent
    `maintain()` call imports the transaction from mempool into a newly-built view
    before `submit_and_watch` gets to submit to that view.

    The fix:

    - `submit_and_watch_inner` now pre-creates the external watcher before mempool
      insertion, so events emitted by a concurrently-created view are not missed.
      On failures the watcher is explicitly removed and inserted mempool entries
      are cleaned up as before.
    - All submission paths (`submit_and_watch_inner`, `submit_at_inner`,
      `submit_local`) capture the set of active view hashes before mempool
      insertion and pass it to the `ViewStore` submission functions.
    - `ViewStore` interprets `AlreadyImported` errors reported by individual views
      against that set: an error from a view created during the submission process
      is the benign maintain-race and is ignored (the transaction was already
      imported into that view from the mempool), while an error from a
      pre-existing view indicates a views/mempool inconsistency and is propagated,
      with a warning logged.

    This avoids returning spurious RPC 1013 for the race case while still
    rejecting transactions that are already known to the pool.

crates:
- name: sc-transaction-pool
  bump: major
